! Na Fir-Chlis – a Nord i3wm theme · lundie.io
!
! X resources – xterm, themed to match the Alacritty palette exactly.
! Merged by x/.xinitrc at session start; a machine-local ~/.Xresources.local is
! merged after it, so per-machine settings (usually faceSize, which varies with
! monitor DPI) stay out of the repo.
!
! Nothing here is read at runtime – xterm samples the database when it starts.
! After editing, run `xrdb -merge ~/.Xresources`; already-open windows keep the
! colours they launched with.
!
! Resources are set on the XTerm class with a loose binding, so they reach the
! scrollbar and menus as well as the terminal itself. `utf8` is on, which is the
! only thing uxterm would have bought us – plain xterm is enough.

! --- Nord palette – canonical · https://www.nordtheme.com/ -------------------
! Polar Night nord0 as the ground, Snow Storm nord4 as the text.

XTerm*background:         #2E3440
XTerm*foreground:         #D8DEE9
XTerm*cursorColor:        #D8DEE9

! Selection: Snow Storm nord6 on Polar Night nord2. Both have to be set –
! xterm falls back to reverse video when highlightTextColor is missing.

XTerm*highlightColor:     #434C5E
XTerm*highlightTextColor: #ECEFF4

! Normal – Aurora for the six hues, Polar Night nord1 as black.

XTerm*color0:             #3B4252
XTerm*color1:             #BF616A
XTerm*color2:             #A3BE8C
XTerm*color3:             #EBCB8B
XTerm*color4:             #81A1C1
XTerm*color5:             #B48EAD
XTerm*color6:             #88C0D0
XTerm*color7:             #E5E9F0

! Bright – Nord has no brighter Aurora, so the six hues repeat and only the
! greys and cyan shift. That is the palette behaving as designed, not an
! oversight: nord3 lifts black, nord6 lifts white, nord7 lifts cyan.

XTerm*color8:             #4C566A
XTerm*color9:             #BF616A
XTerm*color10:            #A3BE8C
XTerm*color11:            #EBCB8B
XTerm*color12:            #81A1C1
XTerm*color13:            #B48EAD
XTerm*color14:            #8FBCBB
XTerm*color15:            #ECEFF4

! --- Font -------------------------------------------------------------------
! FiraCode Nerd Font, matching Alacritty and the bar. faceSize is set here
! rather than left out – xterm has no graceful "unset" – so override it in
! ~/.Xresources.local on a machine where 12pt is wrong.

XTerm*faceName:           FiraCode Nerd Font
XTerm*faceSize:           12

! --- Behaviour --------------------------------------------------------------
! termName advertises 256 colours, without which the palette above is wasted.
! internalBorder matches the 8px padding set in alacritty.toml. bellIsUrgent
! sets the window urgency hint, which the i3 bar picks up as a workspace
! highlight.
!
! Note that xrdb runs this file through cpp, so a stray apostrophe in a comment
! is read as an unterminated string and warns on every session start. Keep the
! prose free of them.

XTerm*termName:           xterm-256color
XTerm*utf8:               true
XTerm*internalBorder:     8
XTerm*scrollBar:          false
XTerm*saveLines:          10000
XTerm*metaSendsEscape:    true
XTerm*selectToClipboard:  true
XTerm*bellIsUrgent:       true
